  "tests": {
    "before": "Two targeted regressions fail against119 product code: fresh packets cannot start the hold/repair with slow or presentation-only complete-frame feedback, and a legacy-cadence wake ends an active hold early. Exact failure log retained.",
    "after": "198 packaged bridge tests pass in the isolated target SDK, including received/presented modes, old-flight guard separation and a bounded hold across an ACK wake.",
    "worker": "120 worker is byte-identical to117/119 (f433e3b2d244f046ba50574801f51fbbb519d2cd6c9d2251a36fba7346d0bc14); previously passing CPP core tests still cover the unchanged code."
  },
  "implemented": [
    "Fresh authenticated packet feedback may drive one bounded pre-RTP hold and a confirmed cropped-rate refresh independently of full-frame receipt cadence or presented/received kind. Packet freshness, actual queue evidence, severe canonical path decrease, worker capability and all-viewer crop readiness remain required for repair.",
    "Retained old-flight window arithmetic still requires its original rapid received-frame contract. Packet evidence cannot acknowledge a complete image/layout or invent delivered bytes.",
    "A legacy-cadence ACK wake cannot end an active packet-evidenced hold early; its existing bounded deadline remains. Ordinary codec dwell/quiet, fixed full-desktop quality, actual byte debt and private-only opcode routing remain."
  ],
