  "diagnosis": {
    "first119": "The first LXC119 profile fails source-age excess at500.770ms. At its canonical cut, the logged rapid-frame age is1.757s; this alone suppresses the119 repair guard. Encoded P-frames continue at the old codec target and an ordinary IDR follows about600ms later. Packet freshness at that exact first cut was not logged, so no exclusive causal claim is made.",
    "diagnostic119": "A separate passive diagnostic repeat passes at231.349ms and records3109 real transport-cc reports with Debian aiortc1.11.0. This disproves a general lack of transport-cc support in that installed library; no dependency upgrade is made. The original failed profile remains a failure.",
    "live120_presented": "The browser runs the genuine shipped presentation-only fallback with RTCRtpScriptTransform made unavailable in this test context. All observed frame-feedback kinds are presented; real transport-cc remains active. A fresh packet-confirmed8000->1813 cut emits a token1/1250kbit/s independent picture31477B after17.78ms.119 would suppress this repair solely because rapid received-frame feedback is absent.",
    "limits": "The changed120 eligibility is deterministically exercised by unit tests and the presentation-only live profile. Normal unseeded119/120 metrics are not a controlled causal decomposition of every latency difference."
  },
